ShortDescription: A free software-defined radio receiver for Windows with a spectrum and waterfall, a scanner, recording, a map and 43 plugins.
Description: FoxSDR is a software-defined radio receiver. It shows the spectrum and waterfall and demodulates NFM, WFM, AM, DSB, USB, LSB and CW, with stereo FM and RDS, a scanner, an airband monitor, audio and I/Q recording, a map and radar scope for decoded aircraft and ships, and plugins from an in-app catalogue. Most radios are driven by FoxSDR's own drivers. With no radio attached, a built-in signal generator and I/Q file playback work. Free for noncommercial use; commercial use needs a separate licence.
